From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:06:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: Add a contrast autofocus algorithm

Sweep the lens over its useful range in coarse steps, stopping once
past the contrast peak, then in fine steps around the best position,
and park it there. The range comes from the lensMin and lensMax limits
of the tuning file: the lens driver exposes its whole DAC range, of
which a module only uses a fraction. In a dark or featureless scene,
where the best contrast is less than 15% above the worst, park the lens
mid-range instead.

A lasting change of the contrast or of the brightness of the focus
window (15 frames) followed by a steadier scene (10 frames) is a scene
change. After one, probe one step on each side of the current position
and climb towards the sharper one, refining at the end, or stay put if
neither side is better: a full sweep after every scene change makes
the lens hunt visibly. The full sweep remains for the first focus.

Enable the algorithm in the uncalibrated tuning file: it does nothing
on cameras without a focus lens.

Assisted-by: LLM
